cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Documented, accepted, honoured: an audit of decoding parameters on hosted
  LLM inference APIs
message: If you use this software or its data, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "the sampler-confound authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hjyi2027/sampler-confound"
abstract: >-
  An instrument and dataset for auditing what hosted LLM inference APIs do with
  decoding parameters: what the vendor documents, what the API accepts, and what
  the output distribution shows was honoured, measured per (provider, model,
  parameter) with a permutation test, a positive control and a calibrated
  negative control. Includes a determinism probe at temperature 0 and the raw
  completions needed to re-derive every verdict.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - decoding
  - inference providers
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-23"
